<title>FRANCE: AGF looks at options on 47 pct owned SAFR.</title>
<headline>AGF looks at options on 47 pct owned SAFR.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer AGF said it had asked Schroders bank to look into the strategic alternatives concerning its 47 percent stake in reinsurer SAFR.</p>
<p>It said in a brief statement that insurer Athena was doing likewise concerning its 10 percent stake in SAFR, or Societe Anonyme Francaise de Reassurance.</p>
<p>SAFR's 1995 net attributable profit was 320 million francs, up 43 percent on the year before and the group predicted in April that its 1996 result should rise by about 10 percent.</p>
<p>AGF sold of most of its stake in reinsurer Scor earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
